# ── TRACK SEPARATION GATE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These four files carry application-domain content that does not belong in this
# public repo. They are untracked today; without these entries a routine
# `git add .` would publish them. One of them quotes a specific third-party
# document that is not public anywhere.
# A rule in a comment is documentation; these lines are the gate.
agent/anaphor_resolver.py
agent/confabulation_shape_detector.py
tests/test_m118_d_referent_binding.py
tests/test_m118_e_canonical_retrieval_miss.py

# graphify-out/ — code-graph BUILD CACHE, ~94 MB, untracked in all 12 repos.
# Also a track-separation hazard by a side door: it INDEXES THE SOURCES, so it
# can carry the content of the four gated files above. Gating the sources does
# not gate their index.
graphify-out/
